- **M43 �?" L2.** At the second occurrence, inside `W_MASK1`:

  ```c
  /* Before */
  uint64_t v = idata & 0xfff00000ULL, f = v >> 20;
  /* After */
  uint64_t v = idata & 0xfffff000ULL, f = v >> 20;
  ```

  This additionally preserves bits **12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19** in `v`. It changes neither `f` nor the acceptance decision. I enumerated all **4,096 fields A- 256 combinations of those eight bits: 1,048,576 cases, zero field differences**.

  Its observable defect is the extra bits in stored readback. The acceptance guard remains, while filtering of the `v` its body stores is partly nulled: clause (d)�?Ts repair-mask case.

- **M44 �?" L2.** At the second occurrence:

  ```c
  /* Before */
  f = v >> 20;
  /* After */
  f = idata >> 20;
  ```

  `v` remains correctly masked. Validation now includes input bits **63:32**, which the fix deliberately removes before testing. This can decline a valid normalized field and retain the previous register value.

  This is an operand substitution within the edited write path: `idata` is already read there, including by the decline body. The field predicate still controls the repaired store. It is inside (d), although describing its effect as �?owidening acceptance�?? would be wrong.

- **M47 �?" L2.**

  ```c
  /* Before */
  d->window_base_1 = idata & (IOC_W_BASE_W_BASE | IOC_W_BASE_SG | IOC_W_BASE_WEN);
  /* After */
  d->window_base_1 = idata & (IOC_W_BASE_W_BASE | IOC_W_BASE_SG | IOC_W_BASE_WEN | (1ULL << 34));
  ```

  The combined mask changes from **`0x3fff00000` to `0x7fff00000`**. Reserved bit 34 becomes stored.

  The new filtering repair is weakened under the existing BASE1 write branch. The WEN announcement condition is unchanged�?"and occurs **after** the store, so that condition is not the justification for inclusion.

These classifications follow the �?oguard kept, repair nulled�?? rule and this instrument�?Ts explicit per-arm store-mask contract. They do not require treating every edited statement as a predicate. None touches an unchanged `W_T_BASE` arm. See the [repair implementation](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_lca.c:377), [clause (d)](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/tools/CLAUDE.md:1287), and [frozen contract](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/lcabadval/killtable_20260910/t4/lca_badval_probe.REPAIRED67.asrun.py:338).

**All three have guest-visible discriminators.** The handler reads `window_mask_1` or `window_base_1` directly into `odata`, then returns its bytes through `memory_writemax64`. Guest quadword reads therefore expose the changed state. Unimplemented DMA translation does not erase that channel.

The HRM specifies unpredictable hardware readback for WO registers. These rows test the emulator�?Ts explicit echo behavior, as the instrument itself acknowledges; hardware unpredictability does not make two different emulator readbacks equivalent.

I exhaustively enumerated the field predicate over `0..4095`. Its 13 accepted fields, in hexadecimal, are:

```text
0, 1, 3, 7, f, 1f, 3f, 7f, ff, 1ff, 3ff, 7ff, fff
