They match [HRM Table 6-6](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/21066_66a_hrm.txt:9581).

The frozen instrument�?Ts complete window-1 write-value sets explain the escapes:

| Register | Values actually written |
|---|---|
| `W_MASK1` | `0x500000`, `0x900000`, `0x3ff00000`, `0xfff00000` |
| `W_BASE1` | `0`, `0x240000000`, `0x340000000` |

MASK1 receives neither low reserved bits nor high reserved bits; BASE1 never receives bit 34.

**Two register/readback rows suffice for the three named mutants**, counting one register oracle per row. Use guest quadword accesses and check both the seed readback and the subsequent transition.

| Register | Seed | Subsequent write | Fixed readback | Mutant readback |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
