codex
Both S5 predictions survive enumeration: among all 4,096 fields, `<= 2` adds only `f=2`; MASK1 never receives that field, and every existing MASK0 write clears bit 12.

There is another gap: MASK0 never accepts a field above `7`. A narrower extraction mask can therefore escape too. I’m checking values that test every stored-mask bit in both windows without adding a row per bit.

