codex
The design is down to five new register-transition rows. A MASK write with every reserved bit set and a normalized field of zero can test filtering, field-source selection, and zero acceptance together. Checking an all-field-bits seed first also catches narrowing.

I also found that BASE1 lacks a silence check. Keeping all new BASE writes WEN-clear lets one shared silence assertion cover both windows in the same new session.

