Use these five transitions. **Each scored row checks the pair `(seed readback, final readback)`**, so the seed check adds no separate scored row.

| Row | Register / IOC offset | Seed, also expected seed readback | Subsequent write | Fixed final readback | Discriminating mutant result |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
| **R1 `wmask0 filter`** | MASK0 `+0x140` | `0xfff00000` | `0xffffffff000fffff` | `0` | Mask `0xfff01000`: **`0x1000`**. Mask `0x7ff00000`: seed reads **`0x7ff00000`**. |
| **R2 `wmask1 filter-zero`** | MASK1 `+0x160` | `0xfff00000` | `0xffffffff000fffff` | `0` | M43: **`0xff000`**. M44 or normalized-zero rejection: retains **`0xfff00000`**. |
